      1
    ],
    "text": "\u5fae\u4fe1\u516c\u4f17\u53f7\uff1a\u6570\u5b66\u6a21\u578b"
  },
  {
    "block_id": "b000012",
    "issues": [],
    "kind": "heading",
    "repairs": [],
    "section_id": "s0003",
    "source_line_ids": [
      "p0001-n0011-l0000"
    ],
    "source_pages": [
      1
    ],
    "text": "Summary"
  },
  {
    "block_id": "b000013",
    "issues": [],
    "kind": "prose",
    "repairs": [
      {
        "left": "p0001-n0012-l0000",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-n0012-l0001"
      },
      {
        "left": "p0001-n0012-l0001",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-n0012-l0002"
      }
    ],
    "section_id": "s0003",
    "source_line_ids": [
      "p0001-n0012-l0000",
      "p0001-n0012-l0001",
      "p0001-n0012-l0002"
    ],
    "source_pages": [
      1
    ],
    "text": "As the productivity has developed rapidly since last century, people have been paying more and more attention to their spiritual life. As an important part of art and culture, music also changes as times goes by, produces many branches and gains popularity all over the world."
  },
  {
    "block_id": "b000014",
    "issues": [],
    "kind": "prose",
    "repairs": [
      {
        "left": "p0001-n0013-l0000",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-n0013-l0001"
      }
    ],
    "section_id": "s0003",
    "source_line_ids": [
      "p0001-n0013-l0000",
      "p0001-n0013-l0001"
    ],
    "source_pages": [
      1
    ],
    "text": "In this paper, we systematically study in\ufb02uence of music through networks and our work can be summarized as following:"
  },
  {
    "block_id": "b000015",
    "issues": [],
    "kind": "prose",
    "repairs": [
      {
        "left": "p0001-n0014-l0000",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-n0014-l0001"
      }
    ],
    "section_id": "s0003",
    "source_line_ids": [
      "p0001-n0014-l0000",
      "p0001-n0014-l0001"
    ],
    "source_pages": [
      1
    ],
    "text": "\u2022 In Problem 1, we construct the in\ufb02uence network as a directed graph, and propose an overall measure for music in\ufb02uence based on several metrics of the network."
  },
  {
    "block_id": "b000016",
    "issues": [],
    "kind": "title",
    "repairs": [],
    "section_id": "s0003",
    "source_line_ids": [
      "p0001-n0003-l0000"
    ],
    "source_pages": [
      1
    ],
    "text": "\u5fae\u4fe1\u53f7\uff1aMATHmodels"
  },
  {
    "block_id": "b000017",
    "issues": [],
    "kind": "prose",
    "repairs": [
      {
        "left": "p0001-n0015-l0000",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-n0015-l0001"
      }
    ],
    "section_id": "s0003",
    "source_line_ids": [
      "p0001-n0015-l0000",
      "p0001-n0015-l0001"
    ],
    "source_pages": [
      1
    ],
    "text": "\u2022 In Problem 2, we analyze the correlation between music features and propose to measure the distance and similarity of music in a latent space by using factor analysis."
  },
  {
    "block_id": "b000018",
    "issues": [],
    "kind": "prose",
    "repairs": [
      {
        "left": "p0001-n0016-l0000",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-n0016-l0001"
      },
      {
        "left": "p0001-n0016-l0001",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-n0016-l0002"
      }
    ],
    "section_id": "s0003",
    "source_line_ids": [
      "p0001-n0016-l0000",
      "p0001-n0016-l0001",
      "p0001-n0016-l0002"
    ],
    "source_pages": [
      1
    ],
    "text": "\u2022 In Problem 3, we discuss the similarity, in\ufb02uence and relation within genre and between genres, propose to distinguish genre by outlier detection, and describe the process of genre changing over time."
  },
  {
    "block_id": "b000019",
    "issues": [],
    "kind": "prose",
    "repairs": [
      {
        "left": "p0001-n0017-l0000",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-n0017-l0001"
      },
      {
        "left": "p0001-n0017-l0001",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-n0017-l0002"
      }
    ],
    "section_id": "s0003",
    "source_line_ids": [
      "p0001-n0017-l0000",
      "p0001-n0017-l0001",
      "p0001-n0017-l0002"
    ],
    "source_pages": [
      1
    ],
    "text": "\u2022 In Problem 4, we show by correlation analysis that reported in\ufb02uncers really affect the style of followers. We also \ufb01nd acousticness and valence, which just correspond to the \ufb01rst latent variable, are more contagious."
  },
  {
    "block_id": "b000020",
    "issues": [
      "hyphen_join_review"
    ],
    "kind": "prose",
    "repairs": [
      {
        "left": "p0001-n0018-l0000",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-n0018-l0001"
      },
      {
        "left": "p0001-n0018-l0001",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-n0018-l0002"
      },
      {
        "left": "p0001-n0018-l0002",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-n0018-l0003"
      }
    ],
    "section_id": "s0003",
    "source_line_ids": [
      "p0001-n0018-l0000",
      "p0001-n0018-l0001",
      "p0001-n0018-l0002",
      "p0001-n0018-l0003"
    ],
    "source_pages": [
      1
    ],
    "text": "\u2022 In Problem 5, based on the strategy of Bollinger Bands, we identify the signals of revo- lutions as those points outside the band. We observe strong signals of revolution in the 1960s and discover that Nat King Cole and The Beatles are the best representatives of revolutionary during this period."
  },
  {
    "block_id": "b000021",
    "issues": [],
    "kind": "prose",
    "repairs": [
      {
        "left": "p0001-n0019-l0000",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-n0019-l0001"
      },
      {
        "left": "p0001-n0019-l0001",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-n0019-l0002"
      },
      {
        "left": "p0001-n0019-l0002",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-n0019-l0003"
      }
    ],
    "section_id": "s0003",
    "source_line_ids": [
      "p0001-n0019-l0000",
      "p0001-n0019-l0001",
      "p0001-n0019-l0002",
      "p0001-n0019-l0003"
    ],
    "source_pages": [
      1
    ],
    "text": "\u2022 In Problem 6, we think some artists of high in\ufb02uence and popularity might lead the trend of genre development. Therefore, we select the dynamic in\ufb02uencer according to these two indicators and show by visualization that genre leaders do play a guiding role and interact with the whole genre closely."
  },
  {
    "block_id": "b000022",
    "issues": [],
    "kind": "prose",
    "repairs": [
      {
        "left": "p0001-n0020-l0000",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-n0020-l0001"
      },
      {
        "left": "p0001-n0020-l0001",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-n0020-l0002"
      }
    ],
    "section_id": "s0003",
    "source_line_ids": [
      "p0001-n0020-l0000",
      "p0001-n0020-l0001",
      "p0001-n0020-l0002"
    ],
    "source_pages": [
      1
    ],
    "text": "\u2022 In Problem 7, we discuss the sociality of music using the music revolution in the 1960s raised by the counterculture movement as an example. We also explore the signi\ufb01cant and possible in\ufb02uence of Internet."
  },
  {
    "block_id": "b000023",
    "issues": [],
    "kind": "prose",
    "repairs": [
      {
        "left": "p0001-n0021-l0000",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-n0021-l0001"
      },
      {
        "left": "p0001-n0021-l0001",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-n0021-l0002"
      }
    ],
    "section_id": "s0003",
    "source_line_ids": [
      "p0001-n0021-l0000",
      "p0001-n0021-l0001",
      "p0001-n0021-l0002"
    ],
    "source_pages": [
      1
    ],
    "text": "Finally we conduct sensitivity analysis on the hyper-parameters used in our model, which proves the stability of our model and shows the rationality of our choice for hyper-parameters. The pros and cons of our model are discussed deeply as well."
  },
  {
    "block_id": "b000024",
    "issues": [],
    "kind": "keywords",
    "repairs": [],
    "section_id": "s0003",
    "source_line_ids": [
      "p0001-n0022-l0000"
    ],
    "source_pages": [
      1
    ],
    "text": "Keywords: Social network, Factor analysis, Correlation analysis, Bollinger Bands, Music evo-"
